[32m+[m[32m### Request Routes[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Method | Path | Access and behavior |[m
[32m+[m[32m| --- | --- | --- |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `GET` | `/requests` | Authenticated list; students see their own requests, administrators see all. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `POST` | `/requests` | Students create a request; server sets owner, requester identity, and `pending` status. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `GET` | `/requests/{serviceRequest}` | Owner or administrator only; another student's record returns 404. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `PATCH` | `/requests/{serviceRequest}/status` | Administrator only; accepts `pending`, `approved`, or `rejected`. |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBrowser requests render escaped Blade pages and use CSRF-protected forms.[m
[32m+[m[32mJSON clients can request JSON responses using the `Accept: application/json`[m
[32m+[m[32mheader. The status form uses PATCH method spoofing and submits through the same[m
[32m+[m[32mauthenticated, policy-protected route.[m
